# `helm package` output. A release packages in CI and nothing here commits a
# parent tarball, but one lands in the working tree the moment somebody runs
# `helm package chart` by hand — which this repository's own test suite does.
*.tgz

# THE RESOLVED SUBCHARTS ARE COMMITTED, and this repository is the ONE place in
# the estate where that is true. Its sibling `yadgarhq/config` ignores
# `chart/charts/` outright, and copying that line here would have been silent
# and fatal.
#
# The reason is measured rather than stylistic. `ci-release.yaml`'s `chart` job
# runs `helm package chart` with NO `helm dependency update` in front of it, and
# `helm package` REFUSES a chart whose declared dependencies are absent:
#
#   Error: found in Chart.yaml, but missing in charts/ directory:
#   config, gateway, iam, iam-db, project, project-db, task, task-db
#
# Every other chart in this estate is a leaf, so that job has never had to
# resolve anything. This is the first parent, and with `chart/charts/` ignored
# its release would fail at the package step with nothing published.
#
# The negation is why the directory line is ABSENT rather than negated: git does
# not reconsider a file whose parent directory is excluded, so `chart/charts/`
# followed by `!chart/charts/*.tgz` would ignore the tarballs anyway.
!chart/charts/*.tgz

# Python bytecode, which `scripts/tests/` produces the first time it runs. The
# pin gate and its suite are the only Python here and neither is packaged.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Scratch PR-body files agents write while reviewing. Ignored here, in the
# repository, instead of relying on a contributor's machine-wide git config —
# that cover exists on one machine and reaches no other clone, no CI, and no
# other contributor.
.local-review/
